# Line-ending and content-type policy for the whole tree.
#
# Pins the policy explicitly instead of leaving git to re-guess it every status
# check under core.autocrlf — the guess can false-positive a byte-identical
# file as "modified" (seen repeatedly on desktop-studio/src-tauri/Cargo.toml).
#
# Every tracked text file in this repo is already stored LF-clean in the index,
# so the catch-all below codifies what is already true rather than rewriting
# anything: `git add --renormalize .` stages nothing. It changes one thing only
# — a checkout now writes LF into the working tree instead of CRLF, whatever
# the contributor's core.autocrlf says.
#
# The reason it is worth having: #211 rewrote dem-patch/src/lib.rs wholesale to
# CRLF, and combined with two raw NUL bytes it also introduced, git reclassified
# the file as binary. The diff became unreviewable ("Binary files differ") and
# the merge became a conflict with no markers written into the file, since git
# will not attempt a textual merge on a binary path. The rule below prevents the
# line-ending half of that outright.

# `text=auto`, not a bare `text`: git still sniffs for NUL bytes and leaves
# genuinely binary content alone. A forced `text` would corrupt the UTF-16
# files listed further down, so do not "simplify" this to `* text eol=lf`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Kept from the original policy. Redundant under the catch-all, but harmless,
# and TOML is the case the false-positive was actually observed on.
*.toml text eol=lf

# ── Valve's own shipped game files ───────────────────────────────────────────
# UTF-16LE with CRLF, exactly as the engine ships them, and parsed by
# analysis::localization::read_to_string_lossy_utf16_or_utf8, which sniffs the
# BOM. `text=auto` would already detect these as binary via their NUL bytes,
# but state it explicitly rather than trusting a heuristic: a mangled one of
# these fails at runtime with wrong strings, not at build time where it would
# be noticed. localizations/dod_tools_english.txt is ours and is UTF-8 — it
# deliberately does not appear here.
localizations/dod_english.txt     binary
localizations/gameui_english.txt  binary
localizations/valve_english.txt   binary

# ── Binary assets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.png    binary
*.ico    binary
*.icns   binary

# GoldSrc demo files. dem-patch/src/tests/demotest.dem arrives with #211 and is
# the first tracked one; listing the extension now means it can never be
# line-ending-mangled on the way in.
*.dem    binary
